Description: Allow a backslash-escaped newline inside strings
 Twig's REGEX_STRING and REGEX_DQ_STRING_PART use PHP's /s flag, so the
 escape "\\." also matches a backslash followed by a line break, as in
 'first \<newline>second'. In JavaScript "." never matches a line break, so
 twig-lexer 1.0.0 throws "Unexpected character" on such strings. The escape
 is written "\\[\s\S]" instead, in both the single/double quoted string
 pattern and the double quoted content pattern. Applies to both levels.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Twig-Reference: none (port fix; /s flag present since Twig 2.x)
Test: test/fixtures/twig/strings.twig (parity with Twig 3.28.0); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-09-23
---
